<title>BELGIUM: EU sets 1997/98 cane sugar import quota.</title>
<headline>EU sets 1997/98 cane sugar import quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union set the 1997/98 (July/June) most-favoured-nation (MFN) raw cane sugar import quota at 85,463 tonnes, European Commission officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 12-months quota, which was approved by the EU sugar management committee on Wednesday, replaces an 18-months quota and corresponds to 82,000 tonnes of white sugar.</p>
<p>It is shared among Cuba (69 percent), Brazil (28 percent) and other countries (3.0 percent) that benefit from a reduced tariff of 98 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>The quota compensates Finland's traditional suppliers under the former General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT) for trade losses after it joined the EU in 1995 and raised tariffs.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
